@garbear I understand your concerns. Although casting each value returned from GetParamX() seems to be an excessive task to implement. m_param1 contains values from constant expressions like GUI_MSG_UPDATE_ITEM, ACTION_SELECT_ITEM. Changing their type to int64_t would introduce inconsistency across other message constants.

I've got two proposals. Please let me know if one of them is acceptable to you (to be honest I'm not a huge fan of them but I didn't come up with anything else).

1. 
```
int CGUIMessage::GetParam1() const
{
  return static_cast<int>(m_param1);
}

int64_t CGUIMessage::GetParam1i64() const
{
  return m_param1;
}

int CGUIMessage::GetParam2() const
{
  return static_cast<int>(m_param2);
}

int64_t CGUIMessage::GetParam2i64() const
{
  return m_param2;
}
```

Narrowing conversion happens in getters - there are no code changes needed from the caller perspective.

2. Leave int in m_paramX and use CGUIMessage::SetPointer/GetPointer to send POD like
```
struct
{
  const int64_t iTime;
  const int64_t seekOffset;
};
```
